# PROJECT.md

Copy this file to `PROJECT.md` at the repository root and replace every placeholder
line with facts about the project before using the flowkit skills.

## Project

- Name: [project name].
- Purpose: [one sentence: what the product does and who uses it].
- Stack: [primary language, frameworks, and toolchains].
- Layout: [where code, tests, docs, and scripts live].

## Status tracking

- Task states: [the exact state values, for example backlog / ready / in progress /
  in review / done]. A blocked task keeps [which state] and records [where the blocker goes].
- Status places: [the files that must always agree — the board, the roadmap, the changelog].
- Task-record template: [path], and where task records are created: [path pattern].
- Issue template: [path]; labels: [the exact label names issues use].
- Changelog: [path], the `[Unreleased]` section, and the exact changelog groups it uses.
- Status commands: [the copy-pasteable command that changes a state, the consistency check,
  and the context command that prints one item's dependencies and open decisions].

## Git & PR

- Base branch: [name]; branch naming: [convention].
- Commit convention: [for example Conventional Commits `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`].
- PR template: [path]; body rules: [what the body must contain].
- Merge command: [the exact command, including how it is pinned to the reviewed head SHA].
- Policy files a human operator reviews before merge: [paths].
- Release and tagging: [who does it, and where the release flow is documented].

## Checks

Every required check as a copy-pasteable command, one line each:
- [test command] — [what it proves].
- [lint / type-check / build].
- [contract lint, generation, and breaking-change check].
- [boundary or import check].
- [status consistency check].

Real environment for verification: [simulator/emulator, workstation, or real device].
Exit-code discipline: a check that was not run is reported as `Not run`, never as passed.

## Docs map

Add one line per document type the skills look up or update:
- Plans: [path].
- Reports and spike evidence: [path]; spike report template: [path].
- Spec, use cases, and design: [paths].
- Copy and UI strings: [path].
- Workflow and process documents: [paths].
- Changelog, roadmap, and board: [paths].
- Scratch and temporary files (agent logs, PR drafts, raw logs): [path].
- Document index: [path].

## Architecture rules

- Architecture law file: [path], including [the rule ids or sections that bind a change].
- Decision records and open questions: [path].
- Hard module and layer boundaries: [who owns logic, which module may import which].
- Single contract source and generated directories: [paths]; never hand-edit generated
  files, never reuse a field, method, or enum number.
- Files or directories that must not change without special review: [paths].

## Quality rules

- Code style: [formatter/linter and the rules that apply].
- Comment language and what a comment may say: [rule].
- Documentation, UI-string, and commit languages: [rule].
- Module boundaries and project-specific constraints beyond the universal skill rules: [rule].
- New dependencies: [the decision record and approval they need].

## PM hooks

Which planning skills apply here, one line each:
- Spec before large or vague work: [when, and where the spec lives].
- Stakeholder updates at milestones: [when, and where they go].
- Roadmap or sprint planning: [when, and where they go].
Delete any line that does not apply to this project.
